{"name":"Whisky Barrel","hex":"#96745b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"whisky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of whiskey, an alcoholic liquor distilled from fermented grain, usually aged in oak barrels,  Scotch; a drink of this liquor. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of whiskey (“a light gig or carriage”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whisky"},{"term":"barrel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A round (cylindrical) vessel, such as a cask, of greater length than breadth, and bulging in the middle, made of staves bound with hoops, and having flat ends (heads). The word is sometimes applied to a similar cylindrical container made of metal, usually called a drum.","Such a cask of a certain size, holding one-eighth of what a tun holds. (See a diagram comparing cask sizes.)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put or to pack in a barrel or barrels.","To move quickly or in an uncontrolled manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barrel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Whisky","blocks":[{"text":"Whisky or whiskey is a type of liquor made from fermented grain mash. Various grains are used for different varieties, including barley, corn, rye, and wheat. Whisky is typically aged in wooden casks, commonly of charred white oak. Uncharred white oak casks previously used for the aging of port, rum, or sherry may be employed during storage to impart a unique flavour and colour."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Whiskyhogmanay2010.jpg/330px-Whiskyhogmanay2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whisky"},{"title":"Barrel","blocks":[{"text":"A barrel or cask is a hollow cylindrical container with a bulging center, longer than it is wide. They are traditionally made of wooden staves and bound by wooden or metal hoops. The word vat is often used for large containers for liquids, usually alcoholic beverages; a small barrel or cask is known as a keg."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg/330px-Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barrel"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Distillerie_OldBushmills.jpg/500px-Distillerie_OldBushmills.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Distillerie_OldBushmills.jpg/1280px-Distillerie_OldBushmills.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Distillerie_OldBushmills.jpg/500px-Distillerie_OldBushmills.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Old Bushmills Distillery, County Antrim","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADistillerie_OldBushmills.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Erskine_Nicol%2C_A_Nip_against_the_Cold_%281869%29.jpg/500px-Erskine_Nicol%2C_A_Nip_against_the_Cold_%281869%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Erskine_Nicol%2C_A_Nip_against_the_Cold_%281869%29.jpg/1280px-Erskine_Nicol%2C_A_Nip_against_the_Cold_%281869%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Erskine_Nicol%2C_A_Nip_against_the_Cold_%281869%29.jpg/500px-Erskine_Nicol%2C_A_Nip_against_the_Cold_%281869%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A man pours some whisky into a flask in this 1869 oil painting by Scottish arti